<header><p class="st-kicker">khanate · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Keraite Khanate</h1><p class="st-meta">1000 CE – 1203 CE (approx.) · capital Orkhon valley</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A powerful Christian steppe khanate in central Mongolia, whose ruler Toghrul was Genghis Khan's patron and rival, and later the model for legends of Prester John.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keraites">Keraites</a> were a large tribal union living along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orkhon-river">Orkhon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuul-river">Tuul</a> rivers in central <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mongolia">Mongolia</a>, probably of Mongolic speech with strong Turkic influences. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syriac">Syriac</a> sources record that their ruler converted to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-the-east">Church of the East</a> around 1007, together with many of his people.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The khanate was a confederation of clans under a ruling family, with Christian priests and Nestorian practices alongside steppe customs. Its rulers, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marghuz-buyruk">Marghuz Buyruk</a>, fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatars">Tatars</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/naiman-khanate">Naimans</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/merkit-confederation">Merkits</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ong-khan">Toghrul</a>, sworn brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Temüjin's</a> father, became the most powerful khan of central <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mongolia">Mongolia</a> and received the title Ong Khan from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/jin-dynasty-1115-1234">Jin dynasty</a> (1115-1234) in 1196 after the campaign against the Tatars.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ong-khan">Toghrul</a> helped the young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Temüjin</a> rise but turned against him; in 1203 Temüjin defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keraites">Keraites</a>, and Toghrul was killed by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/naiman-khanate">Naimans</a> while fleeing. The Keraites joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a>; the Keraite princess <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sorghaghtani-beki">Sorghaghtani Beki</a> was mother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongke">Möngke</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kublai-khan">Kublai</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hulagu-khan">Hülegü</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="khanate, 1000 CE – 1203 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 74 V58 Q50 30 82 58 V74 Z"/><path d="M42 74 V60 H58 V74"/><path d="M30 50 L50 36 L70 50"/><path d="M50 36 V26"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">khanate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:79.60%;width:4.04%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1000 CE – 1203 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>khanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Orkhon valley</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Marghuz Buyruk, Toghrul (Ong Khan)</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Church of the East, Tengrism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Mongolic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mongolia">Mongolia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Keraites, Kerait</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1102&amp;focus=keraite-khanate" aria-label="Keraite Khanate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7138 562 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Keraite Khanate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7866 1006h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7458 818h0"/><path class="map-do